  "result": "All tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause:** In `crates/printer/src/util.rs`, `Replacer::replace_all` extends the `subject` buffer past the match's actual end (`range.end`) by up to `MAX_LOOK_AHEAD` (128) bytes in multi-line mode, so the regex engine can correctly evaluate look-ahead assertions. It then called `Matcher::replace_with_captures_at`, whose generic implementation unconditionally appends everything after the last match (`&haystack[last_match..]`) to the output \u2014 including that extra look-ahead data that was never meant to be part of the actual matched/replaced text.\n\n**Fix:** Replaced the call to `replace_with_captures_at` with a manual search-and-replace loop using `captures_iter_at` that:\n- stops considering matches once they start at or beyond `range.end` (mirroring the existing bound used in `find_iter_at_in_context`), and\n- appends only the trailing unmatched text up to `range.end` (clamped to the buffer length), not the whole extended lookahead buffer.\n\nVerified against the reproduction case from the issue \u2014 output now matches the expected single line, and the full `grep-printer`, `grep-matcher`, and `grep-searcher` test suites (94 + 76 tests) still pass.",
